{title: The Sons Spared}
{subtitle: Exodus 6:24; Numbers 16:1–35; 26:11; 1 Chronicles 6:22–37; 9:19; 6:33–38}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The sons of Korah stand in the line
Assir and Elkanah and Abiasaph
Descendants of Levi in the clan
Holding the history in their hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Abmaj7]The earth opened its mouth wide
[Cm]Swallowing the rebels with pride
But [Abmaj7]the sons of Korah did not [Bb]die
Sparing the lineage from the [Cm]sky
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Korah rose up against Moses
With two hundred and fifty men
They grumbled against God’s choice
Saying we are all holy then
[Abmaj7]Moses fell facedown in the [Cm]dust
As [Abmaj7]the fire from the Lord burst
[Bb]Consuming the incense and the [Ab]proud
While the [Bb]faithful were not al[Cm]lowed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [Abmaj7]earth opened its mouth [Cm]wide
Swallowing the rebels with pride
[Abmaj7]But the sons of Korah did not [Bb]die
Sparing the lineage from the [Cm]sky
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Abiasaph became a father
To Tahath in the Levitical way
His brother Asaph stood right hand
Singing praise for the holy day
The [Abmaj7]Korahites kept the gates
[Cm]Serving where their souls were made
Through [Abmaj7]Abiasaph’s line descended
[Bb]Heman, whose voice was [Cm]blessed
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Abmaj7]Not all who rebel are [Cm]lost
Not [Abmaj7]all who serve are [Cm]crossed
[Abmaj7]The judgment fell on the [Cm]sin
[Abmaj7]But the seed [Bb]remained with[Cm]in
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Abmaj7]sons of Korah [Bb]did not [Cm]die
The [Abmaj7]sons of Korah [Bb]did not [Cm]die
{end_of_verse}
